  "published": "2026-10-12T23:24:16.3Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.0.1: Moves the dependency to CoreSystem.Cache 3.0.1, which depends on CoreSystem.Resilience 2.0.2. That combination is what restores this package on .NET SDK 10 and later: Resilience 2.0.1 pinned Microsoft.Extensions.* to 8.0.x while OpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting 1.19.0 asks for 10.0.0, and the resulting NU1605 broke restore before anything compiled. 3.0.0 cannot be fixed, because published versions are immutable. No public API changed, nothing was renamed, and no code changed here. The AddHealthChecks() prerequisite still applies: RehydrationService takes a HealthCheckService, so without it the host fails to start, and without a primary-tagged check rehydration silently never runs.",
